  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n**\n¶2**\n\n\nImm\neas\nur\nably great is the Divine\n Wisdom\n itself\n to\n all\n who receive\n and\n perce\nive it, by\n virtue\n of the Divine\n Love\n from\n which\n all\n things proceed.\n The\n Divine\n exists\n and\n is established in five\n essential\n fac\nulties of its\n intelligence\n —\n which\n are infinite\n capac\nities that\n have\n neither boundary\n nor end\n —\n namely\n, in\nmost perception, interior\n thought\n, spiritual\n disc\nernment, the\n deliber\nation\n of divine\n purpose\n, and refl\nective wisdom\n in\n act\n. These\n unf\nold further\n into\n the\n complete\n fullness of all divine truths in\n their perfect\n order,\n which\n are\n the twelve degrees\n of wisdom\n proce\neding from the Divine\n.\n\n\n**¶3**\n\nWithin\n each of\n these essential\n faculties of\n divine\n intelligence\n dw\nells the whole\n fullness of all the\n rest\n,\n so\n that each degree contains\n every\n degree\n within itself. From\n each\n,\n living\n truth flows forth abundantly in\n acknowledgment —\n five\n inex\nhaustible out\npourings of wisdom\n, each\n complete\n.\n\n\n**¶4**\n\nThe\n first is the wisdom\n itself\n that\n illumin\nates all things\n —\n the light of divine truth that proceeds\n from the Divine and\n pours forth into every\n state\n of spiritual life without\n exception\n.\n\n**¶5**\n\n\nThe second is the sphere\n of divine good\n as\n it\n is\n in\nward\nly perceived — the frag\nrance of love\n that per\nmeates all states of\n the\n celest\nial kingdom.\n\n\n**¶6**\n\nThe\n third is the Divine\n Truth\n as\n it proceeds\n and\n is\n heard\n — the living Word\n flowing\n through every\n spiritual state and\n ordering\n all things.\n\n**¶7\n**\n\nThe fourth is a\n further\n quality of the\n Divine that\n flows\n forth from the\n in\nmost into\n the outer\n degrees\n.\n (*\nThe\n fragment\n res\nists\n confident\n translation;\n what\n surv\nives indicates\n another\n mode\n of divine influx proce\neding out\nward.\n*)\n\n**¶8**\n\n\nThe fifth is the manif\nested glory\n of the Divine\n Presence — that\n which has\n been revealed\n from\n et\nernity, which continues without\n ce\nasing through\n all states\n.\n This\n glory\n was\n insc\nribed upon the interiors of those who\n receive it\n, and sealed\n within\n them\n —\n impressed\n upon the will and the\n understanding alike\n — so that as\n they transm\nit what\n they have received, they also\n receive spiritual\n nourishment from\n the Divine.\n At\n once the\n living\n Word\n st\nirs within them, heav\nenly joy ar\nises, and everything\n is renewed\n as\n from\n the beginning. Living\n truth\n flows forth contin\nually from within\n, and\n those\n who receive it grow\n rich in goods\n and truths. All\n that\n proceeds\n from this\n state\n is spiritu\nally beautiful —\n an image\n of the Divine stam\nped upon the understanding\n,\n an\n adornment of truth\n clothing\n every\n interior good —\n and those\n who d\nwell in it\n possess\n life\n that\n does\n not end.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "Very great is [the land of] light in the presence of they who will hear and know it, due to the first Father of Greatness. How he ex[ists and is] established in his five light limbs, which are [his infinite store]houses that have neither limit nor measure to the[m. They are] mind, thought, insight, counsel and [consideration. From these proceed] his twelve light limbs that are his twelve wisdoms."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "Now, there are five great light lim[bs] in each one [of them, so that each contains every one within itself; and from each] five grea[t] springs of praise gush for[th; and] five great [rivers of] lig[ht flow forth from them.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "The second is the perfume of the [Father that issues forth] and pervades all the aeons of greatness."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "The third is his living voice of [truth that flows through] all his aeons [and orders all things.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "The fourth is his [sweet]-ness [that] gushes forth from him [and pours o]ut [into all his aeons.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "The fif[th] is his great glorio[us form] that [is revealed, w]hich [has been ma]nifested all the tim[e], whi[ch contin]ues [through] all of them. It was sculpted in them [and was] sealed in the[m; the likeness was] sealed [upon them.] as they send [forth their praise] in [the aeons,] they too receive nourishment [from him.] immediately [they hear his] living voi[ce, and] joy [is] set up anew. It shall gush forth from it [without ceasing, and] they shall [receive it] and become rich in the [light. It] too is beautiful [in its] portray[al, an] adornment [of truth;] and they live [in it] for ev[e]r."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "The first is his light that enlig[htens ... ] it gushed forth from him and pour[ed ... ] a[l]] aeons."
    }
